#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:626 C:\temp11\RodentDialog.cpp:1570
#: C:\temp11\Sound.cpp:1485 C:\temp11\UserBitmap.cpp:824
#: C:\temp11\UserBitmap.cpp:826 C:\temp11\UserBitmap.cpp:947
#: C:\temp11\UserBitmap.cpp:949 C:\temp11\UserBitmap.cpp:1006
#: C:\temp11\UserBitmap.cpp:1008
msgid "to"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:631
msgid "The engine has a repository on GitHub at -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:649
msgid ""
"When < UCI_LimitStrength > is enabled, the engine uses the < UCI_Elo > value"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:651
msgid ""
"to adjust its playing strength. Engines use different algorithms to achieve "
"this,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:653
msgid ""
"such as reducing the search depth, limiting the number of positions examined,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:655
msgid "or adding some randomness to the evaluation function."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:657
msgid "The actual Elo rating achieved by the engine is often an estimate,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:659
msgid "as it's difficult to calibrate precisely."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:661
msgid ""
"You can use this feature to play an engine at a level comparable to your own"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:663
msgid ""
"or to test different engine strengths, even if the exact Elo isn't perfect."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:666
msgid "I have added the < UCI_LimitStrength > option to four engines -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:668
msgid "Gambit Fruit, Toga II, Cyclone Xtreme and Firenzina."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:671
msgid "The method that I have used is based on the code of Ryan Benitez"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:673
msgid "in the Gambit Fruit engine.  He wrote a delay loop governed by the"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:675
msgid "number of nodes (positions) per second that the engine analyses."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:678
msgid "I mapped an Elo rating to a nodes per second value using the following"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:680
msgid "algorithm devised by Ferdinand Mosca"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:683
msgid "nodes_per_second ="
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:688
msgid "I made the addition adjustment in the original formula into a variable"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:690
msgid "< nps_elo_adjustment > in order to fine tune the conversion formula."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:692
msgid "This can be set by the user in engine parameters."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:694
msgid "Increase this value to make the engine stronger,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:696
msgid "decrease it to make the engine weaker."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:699
msgid "Apart from setting the Elo rating, the playing strength"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:701
msgid "of all of these engines can be further adjusted with other options."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:704
msgid "There is also a < Variety > parameter that can be adjusted."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:706
msgid ""
"My intention for this option was that the engine would play a more varied "
"game."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:708
msgid ""
"Then I realised that it could be combined with an < Allowed deficit > option"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:710
msgid "to adjust the engine playing strength further."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:713
msgid "Lines that are weaker than the < Allowed deficit(centi-pawns) >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:715
msgid ""
"when compared to the best move found, are excluded when a move is selected."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:717
msgid ""
"The move that will be played is chosen at random from the remaining moves."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:719
msgid ""
"So raising the value of < Variety > and < Allowed deficit > weakens the "
"engine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:722
msgid "Therefore, if you want the engine to sometimes blunder a rook,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:724
msgid "the upper limit of < Allowed deficit > should be set to 600"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:726
msgid "To occasionally blunder a knight or bishop, it should be set to 350"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:728
msgid "for a pawn it should be about 125."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:731
msgid "You can use the < Variety > option just to vary the play if you set"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:733
msgid "the < Allowed deficit > to a low value, say 25 centi-pawns."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:735
msgid ""
"However, even this will still weaken the engine somewhat because the engine"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:737
msgid ""
"will use the < MultiPV > method of searching, which is slower than normal."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:740
msgid ""
"< Moves to go > is the number of moves that the engine is required to play"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:742
msgid ""
"in whatever time it has remaining.  So if it has 2 minutes, 40 seconds left"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:744
msgid "(160 seconds) and moves to go is set to 40 for that time period,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:746
msgid ""
"it will calculate the time available for its next move as \t160 / 40 = 4 "
"seconds"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\CycloneDialog.cpp:748
msgid "and spend roughly that amount of time \ton its next move."
msgstr ""

