#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:879 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:236
msgid "This allows you to scroll the move list with the middle mouse button,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:881 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:237
msgid "without the position popup box appearing on every move."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:884 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:238
msgid ""
"Popup box check board frequency  -   Input the time interval, in 1/10 of a "
"second,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:886 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:239
msgid "between checks being made for a board position match"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:888 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:240
msgid "when the position popup box is open."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:891 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:241
msgid ""
"Maximum position popup checking time  -  Input the maximum time in seconds"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:893 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:242
msgid "that the position popup box should check for matching boards"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:896 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:243
msgid ""
"Check engine  -  Click this button to see if the UCI engine driver interface"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:898 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:244
msgid "is working properly."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:901 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:245
msgid "Deactivate engine  -  If the E-board becomes out of sync with the GUI,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:903 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:246
msgid "sometimes your only recourse is to disconnect the UCI engine driver"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:905 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:247
msgid "with this option and re-connect it again afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:907 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:248
msgid "You can also toggle E-board icon on the toolbar for this purpose."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:912 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:249
msgid "Use the buttons below to browse detailed technical manuals."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:925 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:250
msgid "Electronic Board Driver Guide:"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:927 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:251
msgid "Initial Installation and Setup -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:928 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:252
msgid ""
"1. Download the specific driver package for your chessboard from Graham "
"O'Neill's website -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:930 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:253
msgid "and run his installation utility."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:932 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:254
msgid ""
"2. This creates an installation folder on your PC containing the UCI engine "
"driver file"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:933 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:255
msgid "that the E-board uses to communicate with the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:934 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:256
msgid "e.g., < NUT_ENG.exe > for ChessNut E-boards, < DGT_ENG.exe > for DGT,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:936 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:257
msgid "or  < MCL_ENG.exe > for Millenium."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:938 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:258
msgid ""
"3. Use the file browser in this dialog to point the < UCI Path > field "
"directly to that file."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:941 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:259
msgid "This sets up the UCI engine driver pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:944 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:260
msgid ""
"The system leverages an isolated text pipeline to communicate with the "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:946 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:261
msgid ""
"When a legal physical move is verified by the board sensors, a background "
"token"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:948 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:262
msgid ""
"is delivered, converted into mouse clicks, and committed to the game move "
"tree in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:951
msgid "Connection and hardware status note -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:954 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:264
msgid ""
"Because the driver acts as a virtual bridge, it manages pipeline signals "
"natively."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:956 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:265
msgid ""
"If the physical board locks up, unplugs, or loses power mid-game, simply "
"uncheck"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:958 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:266
msgid ""
"and re-check the < Enable > checkbox to cycle the driver process and force a"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:960 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:267
msgid "clean hardware re-initialisation."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:963 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:268
msgid "Electronic Board Driver Guide"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:977 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:269
msgid ""
"If you use < Setup position > or load a PGN games from disk, this changes"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:978 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:270
msgid "the position in the GUI and puts it out of sync with the E-board."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:979 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:271
msgid "The E-board will repsond with a popup box, prompting you to re-arrange"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:980 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:272
msgid "the pieces on the E-board to match those in the GUI."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:983 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:273
msgid "The system continuously validates board alignment using a combination"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:984 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:274
msgid "of linear sequential move plies and piece FEN hashes."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:985 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:275
msgid "So if you make a jump in a game with a click in the game move list box,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:986 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:276
msgid ""
"or using a game navigation shortcut on the toolbar, the GUI engine driver"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:987 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:277
msgid ""
"will show a position popup box.  When you reset the pieces on the E-board"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:988 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:278
msgid "to match those on the GUI, the box will clear itself."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:990 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:279
msgid "During a game, if the E-board gets out of sync with the GUI position,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:991 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:280
msgid "you can continue the game from the desired position, by using the"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:992 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:281
msgid "< Setup position > option, followed by starting the game again."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:993 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:282
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, this will mean that the move made prior to the setup position,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:994 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:283
msgid "will be lost from the game move list."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:995 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:284
msgid "If you want to keep the moves, then save the game to disk first."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:996 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:285
msgid "Then start a new game in the GUI, reload the game from disk,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:997 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:286
msgid ""
"navigate to the final move in the GUI, reset the pieces on the E-Board to "
"match"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:998 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:287
msgid "and then restart the game."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1000 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:288
msgid ""
"If, for some reason the E-board and GUI positions become totally out of "
"alignment"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1001 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:289
msgid ""
"and the methods given above do not work,  you can always re-align the boards"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1002 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:290
msgid "by moving the E-board pieces back to their starting positions."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1003 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:291
msgid ""
"If even doing this does not work, the last resort is to deactivate the E-"
"board"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1004 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:292
msgid ""
"and then reactivate it,  either from the E-board dialog box, or from the "
"toolbar option."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1006 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:293
msgid "Executing Physical Takebacks -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1007 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:294
msgid ""
"When < Allow legal move takebacks in games > is enabled, lifting a piece and"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1008 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:295
msgid ""
"and moving it back, registers an immediate undo inside the GUI game tree."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1009 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:296
msgid ""
"If you are playing a game against a chess engine, takebacks are usually made "
"in pairs.  "
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1010 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:297
msgid ""
"You take back a move made by the engine, followed by taking back your own "
"move,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1011 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:298
msgid "(often a blunder) and then play a better move.  "
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1012 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:299
msgid "However, it is also possible to take back one of your own moves"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1013 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:300
msgid "before the computer has replied."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1014 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:301
msgid "When you are not playing a game against a chess engine,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1015 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:302
msgid "take backs on the E-board are always possible."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1017 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:303
msgid "Take backs can be used during the opening book phase"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1019 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:304
msgid "if you want the engine to play an alternative book move."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1021 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:305
msgid "After taking back the book move played by the engine, use the option -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1023 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:306
msgid ""
"< Main menu > < Commands > < Resume play > or the keyboard shortcut < Ctrl + "
"R >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1025 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:307
msgid "The engine will then play another book move at random."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1027 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:308
msgid ""
"If you want to choose a book move for the engine, then after the takeback,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1029 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:309
msgid "pick the move for the engine from the green book moves box,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1031 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:310
msgid "which is located at the top right of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1033 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:311
msgid "Then choose < Main menu > < Commands > < Play white / black >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1035 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:312
msgid "depending on the colour you are playing, in order to resume the game."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1037 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:313
msgid ""
"You can use the < Resume play > method when you are out of the opening book,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1039 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:314
msgid ""
"but in this case you are relying on the engine having a variety of play "
"option,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1041 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:315
msgid "if you want it to play a different move."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1044 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:316
msgid "Castling sequence rule :"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1045 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:317
msgid ""
"To successfully execute a physical takeback of a Castling move, you must move"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1046 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:318
msgid "the King back to its original square first, followed by the Rook."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1047 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:319
msgid ""
"Moving pieces out of this strict sequence will break the driver's layout "
"matrix detection."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1049 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:320
msgid "If you open the < Rated game > dialog box when the E-board is active,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1050 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:321
msgid ""
"you will set that it has been readied for a game between the player on the E-"
"board"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1051 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:322
msgid ""
"and a chess engine in the GUI.  You can still select your preferred engine "
"opponent"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1052 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:323
msgid "and its playing strength in the normal way."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1054 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:324
msgid "Inbuilt E-board connection health check :"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1055 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:325
msgid "Electronic hardware can experience sudden connection losses"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1056 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:326
msgid ""
"due to unplugged USB cables, battery depletion, or wireless sleep modes."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1057 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:327
msgid ""
"To prevent silent lockups, the system uses a Proactive Watchdog Monitoring "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1058 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:328
msgid ""
"Every 5 seconds of complete silence, the app drops an invisible diagnostic "
"health probe"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1059 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:329
msgid "down the pipeline to test the hardware."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1060 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:330
msgid ""
"If the hardware fails to respond within 2 seconds, the application safely "
"disassembles"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1061 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:331
msgid "the background processes, restores your default player profile,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1062 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:332
msgid ""
"and displays a temporary notification alert, so you are never left guessing"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1063 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:333
msgid "about whether the E-board is still connected and responding."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1065 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:334
msgid "Playing guide"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1078 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:335
msgid "Using Opening Book Training with the E-Board:"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1080 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:336
msgid ""
"When Opening Book Training mode is enabled, the GUI acts as an interactive"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1081 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:337
msgid "tutor, verifying every move you play on the physical board matrix."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1083 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:338
msgid "Audio-Assisted Training (Eyes on the Board):"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1085 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:339
msgid ""
"To ensure you can focus entirely on the physical pieces without looking up:"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1087 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:340
msgid ""
"Kettle Drum Sound: Plays immediately if you execute an incorrect blunder "
"move."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1089 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:341
msgid ""
"Ping/Tinkle Sound: Plays when a tactical hint is actively displayed on the "
"GUI."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1092 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:342
msgid "Note: Toggle these in < Main menu > < Options > < Sound Effects >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1094 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:343
msgid "or from < Main menu > < Openings > < Training Options >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1097 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:344
msgid ""
"Here is the correction sequence after playing a move that is not in the "
"opening book :-"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1099 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:345
msgid "After making an opening book error you will hear the Kettle drum sound."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1100 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:346
msgid ""
"If the hint sound is set to emit at this stage, you will hear the ping sound "
"as well."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1101 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:347
msgid "Then you should take back the incorrect move on the E-board."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1102 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:348
msgid ""
"If you play another opening book error on the E-board you will hear the "
"error sound again."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1103 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:349
msgid ""
"If you have reached the maximum number of allowed tries, after you take back"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1104 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:350
msgid ""
"the incorrect move on the E-board, the GUI will automatically play a correct "
"move for you"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1105 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:351
msgid ""
"and light up the squares for this move, so you can play it on the E-board."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1106 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:352
msgid ""
"When you play this catch up move, the GUI will respond with the next book "
"move."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1108 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:353
msgid ""
"Alternative moves  -  If you want the GUI to play an alternative book move "
"to the one"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1109 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:354
msgid ""
"it has chosen, first you must play the move on the E-board which it has "
"actually selected."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1110 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:355
msgid ""
"Then take this move back on the E-board, and the GUI will then play a "
"different move"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1114 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:356
msgid ""
"Click < Main Training Help > below to view general opening book training "
"rules."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1117 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:357
msgid "Opening Book Training Guide"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1121 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:358
msgid "Main Training Help"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1148 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:361
msgid "UCI Engine Driver Architecture:"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1150 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:362
msgid ""
"Special thanks to Graham O'Neill for developing and maintaining the highly"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1151 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:363
msgid "versatile suite of universal electronic board driver interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1152 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:364
msgid ""
"His virtual UCI bridging wrapper makes multi-vendor hardware coordination "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1154 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:365
msgid "Asynchronous Pipeline and Integration Engineering -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1156
msgid ""
"Developed in coordination with an Adaptive AI Coding Collaborator - Google "
"Gemini."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1157 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:367
msgid "Features a customized atomic checking engine, thread-safe mutex guards,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1158 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:368
msgid ""
"a linear ply-accounting sensor layout to completely protect the "
"communication pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1159 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:369
msgid ""
"and asynchronous event execution to safeguard against structural race "
"conditions."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1161 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:370
msgid "Thank you for supporting custom chess software innovation!"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EboardDialog.cpp:1163 C:\temp11\Translate.cpp:360
