#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2099
msgid "Another example is < komodo3-64.exe >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2102
msgid "One weak engine is provided. TarraschToyEngine.exe"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2104
msgid "is good enough to be fun but readily beatable for most players."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2106
msgid "It is ideal for blindfold training (see the training options)"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2109
msgid "You can also set three engine options that are useful for human versus"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2111
msgid "engine operation.  Note that not all engines support all these options."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2113
msgid "(the Tarrasch Toy engine doesn't actually support any of them!)"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2115
msgid "If you don't care about these options then leave the default values"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2117
msgid ""
"< ponder off >  < hash size= 64Mbytes >  and  < max cpu cores=1 > in place."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2120
msgid "For this version of the program I have added an extra basic parameter,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2122
msgid ""
"< Limit playing strength > and the accompanying option < Set ELO rating >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2124
msgid ""
"With Stockfish engines, there is an alternative option for weakening the "
"engine,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2126
msgid "called < Skill Level > which can be set using the custom parameters."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2128
msgid ""
"If both options are set, then < Limit playing strength > takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2131
msgid "When writing the < Rated game > feature I found that the Delfi engine"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2133
msgid "needed the limit strength settings placed in the custom parameter list"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2135
msgid "for them to work."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2137
msgid "For the Delfi engine this action will be made automatically."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2139
msgid "If you have this problem with any other engines, then you can check the"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2141
msgid "< Copy to custom parameters > box and the limit strength parameters"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2143
msgid "will be copied across."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2145
msgid ""
"When using the < Rated game > feature, this is enforced for all engines."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2148
msgid ""
"I also found that if you played more than one game with a weakened Stockfish "
"engine"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2150
msgid ""
"and < Copy to custom parameters > was not set, Stockfish reverted to full "
"strength"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2152
msgid ""
"for the second game.  So it is probably best to always have this option set"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2154
msgid "when using limit strength."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2157
msgid ""
"As before, you can still add extra custom parameters by simply typing them "
"in."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2159
msgid ""
"However, to make things easier, I have added an < Engine parameters.. > "
"button"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2161
msgid ""
"which allows the user to display a list of available engine parameters and "
"then"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2163
msgid "select the ones that they require."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2165
msgid "There are also two extra custom parameters now available to use."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2167
msgid ""
"There is a more detailed explanation in the < Engine parameters.. >  help "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2170
msgid "Please exercise caution when using the custom parameters!"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2173
msgid "The engine parameters that have you set, can be saved and loaded"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2175
msgid "using the < Save engine.. > and < Load engine.. > buttons."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2177
msgid "Engine parameter (*.epm) files from previous versions of the program"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2179 C:\temp11\EngineMatchDialog.cpp:1233
msgid "can still be loaded and used in this version, but they will be saved"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2181 C:\temp11\EngineMatchDialog.cpp:1235
msgid "in the new format."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2184
msgid ""
"If you find that eight custom parameters is not enough, then you can check"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2186
msgid ""
"the < Use all parameters > box and when you click on < Engine parameters >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2188
msgid ""
"you will be able to set all engine parameters to the values that you want."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2190
msgid ""
"< Use all parameters > will appear in the first slot of custom parameters."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2192
msgid ""
"It will only be set to true after you have accessed the < Engine parameters >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2194
msgid "dialog box.  It cannot be set manually."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2196
msgid ""
"It can be cleared with the < Reset > button, or by loading another engine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2200
msgid ""
"If you load an engine from an epm file and want to see this name displayed"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2202
msgid ""
"for engine references in order to differentiate it from the standard engine"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2204
msgid "it is based on, then save the engine epm file with a distinctive name"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineDialog.cpp:2206
msgid "and check the < Use engine epm name > checkbox."
