#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1537
msgid "Endgame tablebases are files containing best play for various endgames."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1539
msgid ""
"They can now cater for endings up to 7 pieces, but as the number of pieces "
"increases,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1541
msgid ""
"so does the file size.  The size of a 7 piece Syzygy tablebase is over 18 "
"Terra bytes."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1543
msgid "A large number of 8 piece positions have also been solved."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1546
msgid ""
"Prior to working on the new engine dialog box, I had never tried using "
"tablebases"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1548
msgid "with this program.  The three that I tried worked fine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1550
msgid "I tested 3-4-5 piece tablebases with various engines."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1552
msgid "The Syzygy tablebase worked with the Stockfish and Komodo engines."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1554
msgid ""
"The two positions I tried from the Nalimov tablebase worked with the Rybka "
"2.3 engine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1556
msgid ""
"The two positions I tried from the Gaviota tablebase worked with the Houdini "
"1.5 engine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1559
msgid ""
"Most modern engines now use the Syzygy tablebases because they are much "
"smaller."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1561
msgid ""
"The 3-4-5 Nalimov and Gaviota tablebases can still be found on the Internet "
"Archive,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1563
msgid "but the download sizes are very large at 7 Giga bytes."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1566
msgid ""
"The size of 3-4-5 Syzygy tablebase is much more reasonable at just under 1 "
"Giga byte."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\EngineOptionDialog.cpp:1568
msgid ""
"For anyone who wants to try this tablebase, I have made a download at these "
"links :-"
msgstr ""

