#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1159
msgid "Making your own videos with the program is not too difficult."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1161
msgid "There are three stages to the process :-"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1164
msgid "1.  Preparing the annotations for the selected game."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1166
msgid "2.  Filming the video."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1168
msgid "3.  Inserting the video markers."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1171
msgid ""
"When preparing the annotations for a game, you can place a pause marker ^p"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1173
msgid "in a comment if you want the program to pause at a certain point."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1175
msgid "These can be used if you want to make the video into a quiz."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1178
msgid ""
"I filmed the video with a smartphone, using modified annotations from the "
"game"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1180
msgid ""
"for the script.  I thought it best to have the quiz questions only in the "
"video,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1182
msgid ""
"so I put them in the annotations to the game to begin with and removed them"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1184
msgid "from the game when filming was complete."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1187
msgid "If you have additional material to add to the video, such as pictures,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1189
msgid ""
"you will need a video editing program.  I used the free program <Openshot>"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1191
msgid "for this purpose but there are plenty of others to choose from."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1193
msgid ""
"Also, I found that the video files were very large, so I used the free "
"program"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1195
msgid "<HandBrake> to shrink them. With the shrinking slider set at halfway,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1197
msgid ""
"the video file shrank by a factor of 10 with hardly any loss of quality."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1199
msgid ""
"It is best to shrink the mp4 file after you have exported it from OpenShot."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1202
msgid ""
"To insert the video markers you need to set the Media Player into edit mode."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1204
msgid "This is done by first selecting <Options> from the Media Player menu,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1206
msgid "then clicking the <Edit mode> checkbox.  Alternatively, you can click"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1208
msgid ""
"on the two headed arrow on the toolbar.  This will automatically switch off"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1210
msgid "the <Update from game> and <Update from video> options, because editing"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1212
msgid "is impossible with these switched on."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1215
msgid ""
"Editing is much easier to do from the toolbar, so you can switch that on"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1217
msgid "while you have the <Options> dialog box open."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1219
msgid ""
"Then you go to the start of the game and video, play the video and pause it"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1221
msgid "when you reach the end of the section that you want."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1223
msgid "Then click on the point in the game move list where that video section"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1225
msgid ""
"should be played and place a video marker by clicking on the orange down "
"arrow"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1227
msgid "on the toolbar or selecting <Set video marker> from the edit menu."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1230
msgid ""
"There are some technical issues relating to placing markers for annotations"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1232
msgid "or for quiz questions in a game designed to be used in puzzle mode."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1235
msgid "The first arises when the move played in the main line is dubious"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1237
msgid "and you want to ask the user if they can find a better move"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1239
msgid "which is placed in a sub-variation."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1241
msgid "This means that if main line move is chosen by the user in puzzle mode,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1243
msgid "it should be taken back by the program and the user allowed"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1245
msgid "to have another try, up to the maximum number of tries allowed."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1247
msgid ""
"This is achieved by placing a ^p marker in a comment before the quiz move"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1249
msgid "and a ^b backup marker in a comment after the move to be taken back."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1251
msgid ""
"The backup one move process with a ^b marker only functions in puzzle mode."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1253
msgid "You can see an example of how to do this in the London-Ediburgh game"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1255
msgid "with the moves 24... g5 and 25. Rf5 in the main line."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1258
msgid ""
"The second issue concerns the placement of ^p and ^b markers in comments."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1260
msgid ""
"If the comment is less than 255 characters, then the marker can be placed"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1262
msgid "at the end of the comment, otherwise it has to go at the start."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1264
msgid "This only becomes an issue if a user adds their own annotations"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1266
msgid "to an existing game. There is, of course, no need to count the number"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1268
msgid "of characters in a comment.  Just place the ^p or ^b at the start"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1270
msgid "of the comment if there is any doubt."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1273
msgid ""
"The third issue arises when you want to place a quiz question in the first "
"move"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1275
msgid ""
"of a sub-variation which branches from a move which also has a quiz question."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1277
msgid ""
"In order to do this, you have to make the stem move a sub-variation of "
"itself,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1279
msgid "and then put the ^p marker in a comment to the duplicate sub-variation."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1281
msgid ""
"The identical sub-variation is created by clicking on the start of another"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1283
msgid "sub-variation before it is played and then playing the stem move again."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1285
msgid ""
"It will be neccessary to create a temporary sub-variation for this purpose"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1287
msgid "if none currently exist.  This can be deleted afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1289
msgid ""
"The subsequent answering move, with a comment containing a video marker,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1291
msgid "must also be placed here as well."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1293
msgid "An example of this can be seen in the London - Edinburgh game"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1295
msgid "with moves 26... Qxc4 and 26... bxc4 in the sub-variation to 25. Rf5"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1297
msgid "Another example is the sub-variation 40. Rf3"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1299
msgid "which stems from 40. g4 in the main line."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1302
msgid ""
"The fourth issue is about the placement of markers.  Although it is possible"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1304
msgid ""
"to place a marker after a move, it is much easier to place them in comments."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1306
msgid "Also, if you want to allow for annotations to be added to a game that"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1308
msgid ""
"accompanies a video file, then the game list move element for the marker"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1310
msgid "must be unique. Otherwise there can be problems with game/video"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1312
msgid "synchronization when the game move list is rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1314
msgid "You can see an example of this in the London - Edinburgh game with the"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1316
msgid ""
"move 26. Rxc4 which is present in the 2nd sub-var stemming from 22... h6"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1318
msgid "and also in the 1st sub-var stemming from 25. Rf5"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1320
msgid "So, when making the video, I had to place a marker in a comment"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1322
msgid "after the second instance of 26. Rxc4 for everything to work properly."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1325
msgid ""
"The fifth issue is the placing of annotations to modify puzzle mode sounds."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1327
msgid "After a quiz question, if there is an incorrect move in the main line"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1329
msgid "with a ^b backup move marker in the comment that follows it,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1331
msgid "by default you will get a correct move sound when the move is played."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1333
msgid "This sound effect can be modified by adding a marker to the comment."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1335
msgid "Add ^si for a puzzle incorrect sound and ^sn for no sound at all."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1337
msgid "If the correct puzzle move is in a sub-variation, usually you would get"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1339
msgid ""
"no sound at all when the move is played. If you want to produce a correct"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1341
msgid "move sound here, then add ^sc to the comment following the move."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1344
msgid ""
"Finally, after making or editing a video PGN file, in order for the video"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1346
msgid ""
"to play properly, you have to switch out of edit mode and back into play "
"mode."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1349 C:\temp11\Net.cpp:2099
msgid "IMPORTANT NOTE :"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1351
msgid "Although it is possible to add video markers to an existing game,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1353
msgid "this is not advisable, because unless you were very careful,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1355
msgid "doing so will probably throw off the game/video synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\MediaPlayer.cpp:1357
msgid "and thus make the video useless."
msgstr ""

