#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:788
msgid "Using the move weights in a PolyGlot .bin opening book"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:790
msgid "presents some difficulties.  According to the Polyglot documentation,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:792
msgid "the move weight indicates the likelihood that a move will be played."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:794
msgid "Previously, I had misunderstood how this number was calculated."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:797
msgid "When a move is added to the book, if the game in which it appeared"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:799
msgid ""
"was a win for the colour to play, then the move weight is increased by two."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:801
msgid "If the game was a draw, then the move weight is increased by one."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:803
msgid "So the move weight is an indication of how often a move was played"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:805
msgid "and how it performed."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:808
msgid "Although this method does have some drawbacks, these are mimimized"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:810
msgid "if the book was made using a large number of reasonable quality games."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:812
msgid "However, my previous comment about the move weights in some Polyglot"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:814
msgid ""
".bin opening books not being much use for move filtering is still valid."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:817
msgid ""
"e.g  In the GmOpenings.bin opening book, which is one of the better ones,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:819
msgid ""
"1. e2-e4  gets a weight of 968 and after 1... e7-e5 with a weight of 170"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:821
msgid "the move 2. Nf3 gets a weight of 367 and the alternatives -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:823
msgid "2. f4 (18)  2. Nc3 (9)  2. Bc4 (3)"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:826
msgid "So in order to filter this book so that a move would be played from a"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:828
msgid "certain range, I have made an option for scaling the weights called"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:830
msgid "< Use weight scaling >  This scales the move with the highest weight"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:832
msgid "in the block to the value that you select for the maximum scale weight."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:834
msgid "It then scales the other move weights by the same factor."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:836
msgid "So in the example above, if you set the maximum scale weight to 999"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:838
msgid "then 2. Nf3 will be set to 999  2. f4 (109)  2. Nc3 (54)  2. Bc4 (18)"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:840
msgid "Although this is hardly ideal, it does allow you set a range"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:842
msgid "for the move weights.  For example, if you set a filter range value"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:844
msgid "of  100 - 999  then you will get at least one move at every turn,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:846
msgid "with the lower weight moves filtered out."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:849
msgid "If you just want a move played at random from the opening book then"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:851
msgid "switch off <Use weight scaling> and switch off <Use weight filter>"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:853
msgid "or switch <Use weight filter> on and set the filter min weight to 1"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:855
msgid "and filter max weight to 65000"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:858
msgid "The scaling and filtering options do not alter the move weights"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:860
msgid "in the opening book, the weights are only modified for display."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:862
msgid "If you want to make the move weight scaling and/or filtering changes"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\PolyglotWeightDialog.cpp:864
msgid "permanent, then click on the <Re-write file> button."
msgstr ""

