msgid "The Rodent 4 engine support material, without engines"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:351
msgid "Rodent 3 support material, without engines"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:370
msgid ""
"A Rodent personality file is simply a list of UCI commands in a *.txt file"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:372
msgid "It is supposed to work in the following manner -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:374
msgid ""
"The chess program GUI sends the < Personality > command to the Rodent engine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:376
msgid "The engine then reads the commands from the personality file"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:378
msgid "and adjusts its settings accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:381
msgid "However, with both Nimzo_3d and the Tarrasch GUI,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:383
msgid "I could not get the engines to work when used in this way."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:385
msgid "All of the personalities played the same moves."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:388
msgid ""
"So instead of this, I intercepted the < Personality > command when it was"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:390
msgid ""
"about to be sent from the GUI to the engine , opened the personality file"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:392
msgid "and sent the commands from the file individually.  This seems to work."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:397
msgid ""
"Essentially, the Rodent engine has two main methods of varying its playing "
"strength."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:399
msgid ""
"It can use ELO limit strength or Nodes per seconds with evaluation blur."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:401
msgid "ELO limit strength allows you to set an approximate ELO rating"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:403
msgid "and nodes per second with evaluation blur lets you set values"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:405
msgid "that have a similar weakening effect."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:408
msgid "The Rodent 3 personalities are set up to use nodes per second"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:410
msgid "with evaluation blur and Rodent 4 is intended to be used"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:412
msgid "with ELO limit strength only."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:415
msgid ""
"Because of my modification to the way the < Personality > command is sent,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:417
msgid "Rodent 3 can use its personalities with ELO limit strength"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:419
msgid "in combination with evaluation blur and select skill,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:421
msgid "but not with nodes per second."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:426
msgid "It also means that Rodent 4 can use ELO limit strength"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:428
msgid "with evaluation blur and select skill."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:431
msgid "Changing the evaluation blur value slightly means the engine will play"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:433
msgid "different moves without greatly affecting the playing strength,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:435
msgid "so long as the blur value is not too high."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:436
msgid "You can experiment with this, I found that values between 20 - 50"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:438
msgid "worked quite well."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:443
msgid "As well as that, both engines can now use the personality files"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:445
msgid "of the other engine with only minor adjustments from within Nimzo_3d,"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:447
msgid ""
"once they have been copied into the < Personalities > directory of the "
"engine."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:449
msgid ""
"This allows you to easily swap in new personality files if you want a change."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:451
msgid "I have placed some in < extra_personalities >"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:453
msgid "within the < Personalities > directory."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:456
msgid "The personality files are stored in the following directories -"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:459
msgid "plus"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:459
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:463
msgid "The files can be modified from within Nimzo_3d to adjust the"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:465
msgid ""
"nodes per second and evaluation blur values and then saved back to disk."
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:468
msgid "It does not matter that the personality files can end up with commands"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:470
msgid "that are unsuitable for the engine currently in use, because they are"
msgstr ""

#: C:\temp11\RodentHelp.cpp:472
msgid "filtered out by the GUI before they are sent to the engine."
msgstr ""

